ystem.\n\nStep 3: Caller identity verified\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Identity Verification panel\nAsk the caller for at least 2 of: employee ID, manager's name, department, or last 4 digits of the phone on file. ✅ Do not send a one-time code to the user — your own admin session already satisfies the authentication requirement; this checklist is what verifies the caller is who they claim to be. If fewer than 2 items match, stop and escalate to your team lead rather than proceeding.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 3 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.90 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a CoreID Admin Console page, with a white background and a dark blue sidebar on the left. The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\" and has a list of options below it.\n\n*   **CoreID Admin Console**\n    *   The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n    *   There are two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n    *   There is a text box labeled \"Department matches record\".\n    *   There is a checkbox labeled \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\".\n    *   At the bottom of the page, there is a message that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n\n**Summary**\n\nThe image shows a CoreID Admin Console page with a list of options for verifying an employee's identity. The page has two checkboxes, a text box, and a checkbox, and a message at the bottom indicating that two out of four requirements have been met.\n\n**Detailed Description**\n\n*   **Application**\n    *   The application is CoreID Admin Console.\n*   **Page**\n    *   The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n*   **Layout**\n    *   The page has a white background and a dark blue sidebar on the left.\n*   **UI Elements**\n    *   There are two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n    *   There is a text box labeled \"Department matches record\".\n    *   There is a checkbox labeled \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\".\n*   **Notifications**\n    *   There is a message at the bottom of the page that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n\n**Extracted Text**\n\n*   **Title**\n    *   J. Employee - Identity Verification\n*   **Checkboxes**\n    *   Employee ID matches ticket\n    *   Manager name matches ticket\n*   **Text Box**\n    *   Department matches record\n*   **Checkbox**\n    *   Last 4 digits of phone on file\n*   **Message**\n    *   2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\n\n**Errors and Warnings**\n\n*   **None**\n\n**Likely Issue Category and Severity**\n\n*   **Category**\n    *   Software/application\n*   **Severity**\n    *   Medium\n\n**Observed Facts vs Inference**\n\n*   **Observed Facts**\n    *   The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n    *   There are two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n    *   There is a text box labeled \"Department matches record\".\n    *   There is a checkbox labeled \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\".\n    *   There is a message at the bottom of the page that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n*   **Inference**\n    *   The page is likely used for verifying an employee's identity.\n    *   The checkboxes and text box are likely used to collect information about the employee's identity.\n    *   The message at the bottom of the page indicates that two out of four requirements have been met, suggesting that the verification process is not yet complete.\n\n**Confidence Score and Notes**\n\n*   **Confidence Score**\n    *   0.95\n*   **Confidence Level**\n    *   High\n*   **Confidence Reason**\n    *   The image is clear and well-lit, and the text is legible.\n\nStep 4: Temporary password issued\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Reset Password\nSelect Generate Temporary Password. Leave Force change at next sign-in checked — this is the default and it must not be disabled.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 4 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.80 / Medium]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a password reset page for an employee named J. Employee, with a temporary password provided and a button to generate a new one.\n\n*   **Reset Password - J. Employee**\n    *   The title of the page is \"Reset Password - J. Employee\".\n    *   The page has a white background with black text.\n    *   There is a blue button that says \"Generate Temporary Password\" at the bottom of the page.\n*   **Temporary password**\n    *   The temporary password is displayed in a text box.\n    *   The password is \"Tq7#mVr2IkLp9x\".\n    *   There is a checkbox next to the password that says \"Force change at next sign-in\".\n*   **Generate Temporary Password**\n    *   The button is blue and has white text.\n    *   When clicked, it will generate a new temporary password for the user.\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe image shows a password reset page for an employee named J. Employee, with a temporary password provided and a button to generate a new one. The page has a white background with black text, and the temporary password is displayed in a text box with a checkbox next to it. The button to generate a new temporary password is blue and has white text.\n\n**Detailed Description:**\n\n*   The page has a white background with black text.\n*   The title of the page is \"Reset Password - J. Employee\".\n*   The temporary password is displayed in a text box.\n*   The password is \"Tq7#mVr2IkLp9x\".\n*   There is a checkbox next to the password that says \"Force change at next sign-in\".\n*   The button to generate a new temporary password is blue and has white text.\n\n**Extracted Text:**\n\n*   Reset Password - J. Employee\n*   Temporary password: Tq7#mVr2IkLp9x\n*   Force change at next sign-in\n*   Generate Temporary Password\n\n**Errors and Warnings:**\n\n*   None visible\