n is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.\n\n## LINKED REFERENCE KNOWLEDGE (Scraped from embedded SOP URLs):\n### Reference Web Page [https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world/require-strong-passwords]:\nURL: https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world/require-strong-passwords\nStatus Code: 200\n\n--- SCRAPED MARKDOWN CONTENT START ---\n[Skip to main content](#main)\n\n![U.S. flag](/profiles/cisad8_gov/themes/custom/gesso/dist/images/us_flag_small.png)\n\nAn official website of the United States government\n\nHere’s how you know\n\nHere’s how you know\n\n![Dot gov](/profiles/cisad8_gov/themes/custom/gesso/dist/images/icon-dot-gov.svg)\n\n**Official websites use .gov**\n\n A **.gov** website belongs to an official government organization in the United States.\n\n![HTTPS](/profiles/cisad8_gov/themes/custom/gesso/dist/images/icon-https.svg)\n\n**Secure .gov websites use HTTPS**\n\n A **lock** (LockA locked padlock) or **https://** means you’ve safely connected to the .gov website. Share sensitive information only on official, secure websites.\n\n[Staying Secure at Events](/staying-secure-large-scale-events)[no-cost Cyber Services](/resources-tools/resources/free-cybersecurity-services-and-tools \"Free Cyber Services\")[secure your business](/secureyourbusiness)[Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog](/kev)[Report A Cyber Issue](/report)\n\n[![Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency logo America’s Cyber Security Defense Agency National Coordinator For Critical Infrastructure Security and Resilience](/sites/default/files/images/SVG/header_logo_tagline_update.svg)![Cybersecurity & Infrastructure Security Agency logo America’s Cyber Security Defense Ag