ystem.\n\nStep 3: Caller identity verified\nNavigation: CoreID Admin Console → user profile → Identity Verification panel\nAsk the caller for at least 2 of: employee ID, manager's name, department, or last 4 digits of the phone on file. ✅ Do not send a one-time code to the user — your own admin session already satisfies the authentication requirement; this checklist is what verifies the caller is who they claim to be. If fewer than 2 items match, stop and escalate to your team lead rather than proceeding.\n\n### Visual Inspection Report (Image 3 (inline, following the text above)) [Confidence: 0.90 / High]:\nThe image shows a screenshot of a CoreID Admin Console page, with a white background and a dark blue sidebar on the left. The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\" and has a list of options below it.\n\n*   **CoreID Admin Console**\n    *   The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n    *   There are two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n    *   There is a text box labeled \"Department matches record\".\n    *   There is a checkbox labeled \"Last 4 digits of phone on file\".\n    *   At the bottom of the page, there is a message that says \"2 of 4 confirmed - minimum required to proceed\".\n\n**Summary**\n\nThe image shows a CoreID Admin Console page with a list of options for verifying an employee's identity. The page has two checkboxes, a text box, and a checkbox, and a message at the bottom indicating that two out of four requirements have been met.\n\n**Detailed Description**\n\n*   **Application**\n    *   The application is CoreID Admin Console.\n*   **Page**\n    *   The page is titled \"J. Employee - Identity Verification\".\n*   **Layout**\n    *   The page has a white background and a dark blue sidebar on the left.\n*   **UI Elements**\n    *   There are two checkboxes: \"Employee ID matches ticket\" and \"Manager name matches ticket\".\n    *   There is a text box labele