de the way self-service does?\nThe self-service code exists to authenticate an anonymous claimant with no other proof of identity. Here, identity is established two ways at once: your own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Confirm the ticket category and note the requester's employee ID and manager name.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The SOP explicitly describes reviewing a ticket for employee ID and manager name. The `search_user` function aligns with this action, and the `solandra` platform is active and registered. Required inputs (employee_id) are provided in the SOP.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"search_user\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{{{entities.employee_id}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Verify the caller's identity using the CoreID Admin Console identity verification checklist.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The SOP describes verifying caller identity using at least 2 of 4 items. The `verify_caller_identity` function matches this action, and the `solandra` platform is active. Required inputs (user_id, employee_id, manager_name, department, phone_last4) are mappable from the SOP or prior step outputs.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"verify_caller_identity\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"user_id\": \"{{{{variables.user_id}}}}\",\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{{{entities.employee_id}}}}\",\n      \"manager_name\": \"{{{{entities.manager_name}}}}\",\n      \"department\": \"{{{{entities.department}}}}\",\n      \"phone_last4\": \"{{{{entities.phone_last4}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.account_locked == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 90\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 3,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Generate a temporary password for the locked user and enable force change at next sign-in.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The SOP describes generating a temporary password with force change enabled. The `generate_temporary_password` function matches this action, and the `solandra` platform is active. Required input (user_id) is available from prior steps.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"generate_temporary_password\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"user_id\": \"{{{{variables.user_id}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.identity_verified == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 4,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Resolve the ticket with an audit note detailing the actions taken.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 passed: The SOP describes resolving the ticket with an audit note. The `resolve_ticket` function matches this action, and the `solandra` platform is active. Required inputs (ticket_id, resolution_note) are provided in the SOP or can be constructed from prior outputs.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"resolve_ticket\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"ticket_id\": \"{{{{entities.ticket_id}}}}\",\n      \"resolution_note\": \"Identity verified (2 of 4 checks). Temporary password issued via CoreID. Force-change-at-next-sign-in enabled. No OTP sent - admin-mediated reset per policy.\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.temporary_password != null\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is missing from the OKF steps, you MUST mark `is_faithful = false` and add it to `dropped_commands`.\n  *(HUMAN CONFIRMATION EXEMPTION: Human/verbal/ticket confirmations, user clarifications, and manual admin approval steps are currently PAUSED. DO NOT flag omitted verbal/ticket/user confirmation steps as dropped commands.)*\n  *(GUI SETUP EXEMPTION: GUI setup steps such as \"Open Command Prompt\", \"Press Windows Key\", \"Run as administrator\", \"Open Web Browser\", or opening UI windows are intentionally omitted from executable playbooks. DO NOT flag GUI setup steps or UI window launches as dropped commands.)*\n  *(TOOL PARAMETER MAPPING EXEMPTION: When an automated search or query step maps to a registered API tool whose interface requires a specific input key (such as `search_users` requiring `email`), passing the query entity like `{{entities.email}}` or `{{entities.partial_detail}}` in `comm_inputs` satisfies the step. Do NOT flag other raw search criteria like name or employee ID as dropped commands or parameter inaccuracies when mapping to a catalog tool's defined input parameters.)*\n- **Check 2 (Hallucination Prevention)**: Verify that NO extra CLI commands or fabricated API tool calls were created that were NOT in the raw human SOP text.\n- **Check 3 (Fallback & Parameter Accuracy)**: Verify that fallback commands (`fallback_command`), cross-SOP referrals (`fallback_sop_id`), and tool inputs match the raw text's instructions within the constraints of the registered API tools.\n- **Check 4 (4 Verification Gates & Command Executability Audit)**:\n  * For EVERY `tool_call` step: Verify it satisfies the 4 Gates (Gate 1: matches declared platform function, Gate 2: valid platform, Gate 3: problem aligned, Gate 4: required input parameters present in `comm_inputs`).\n  * For EVERY `command` step: Verify that `command` is an actual executable CLI string and is NEVER null or empty.\n  * Verify that purely manual/verbal/phone relay steps were NOT emitted as empty command steps.\n\n## VERDICT CONTRACT:\n- If all actions are preserved, zero hallucinated commands/tools exist, and all steps are 100% executable, set `is_faithful = true` and `validation_feedback = \"PASSED FAITHFULNESS INSPECTION\"`.\n- If any actions are missing, fabricated, or non-executable, set `is_faithful = false` and populate `dropped_commands` or `hallucinated_commands`.\n\nOutput a valid JSON object matching the JITFaithfulnessInspectionResult schema.\n"
